# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 198-204 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 16 — CHAPTERS 19-21, LEAN, 2026-09-24): the guards with iron mallets, the beginning of defeat
# is flight, the optional war's exemptions against the commanded war's bridegroom (198); optional war, a city not a metropolis nor a village, not by hunger or
# thirst or disease, great is peace with Sihon's messengers (199); all of it, the Canaanites within, tribute and servitude both, the siege's hunger, the males,
# the women and children, Midian's little girls, the spoil (200); the far cities, the seven nations by the sword, the spoil permitted, the Girgashite (201);
# the penitent nations, sinners before the LORD (202); optional war, the city, two and three days, seizing not capturing, the channel diverted, the Sabbath's
# three days and Shammai's ship, eat and cut not, R. Ishmael's fruit, the hindering tree (203); the barren tree first, R. Elazar b. R. Shimon's value, the
# siege-works and the missiles, even on the Sabbath (204). Every row READ WHOLE; the prior reads REREAD WHOLE and marked; the cuts by ch19_ink.SP_.
from ch19_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(198, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WHEN THE OFFICERS HAVE FINISHED" (20:9) — AT THE PEOPLE\'S HEELS THEY STATION GUARDS BEFORE AND BEHIND WITH IRON MALLETS IN THEIR HANDS, AND WHOEVER SEEKS TO TURN BACK THEY MAY BREAK HIS LEGS, FOR THE BEGINNING OF DEFEAT IS FLIGHT — "ISRAEL FLED BEFORE THE PHILISTINES AND A GREAT SLAUGHTER" (1 SAMUEL 4:17). OF WHAT IS THIS SAID? OF AN OPTIONAL WAR; IN A COMMANDED WAR ALL GO OUT, EVEN THE BRIDEGROOM AND THE BRIDE (JOEL 2:16). ({SP_(198, 1, "מעמידים", "זקפים")} "they station guards"; {SP_(198, 1, "וכשילים", "של", "ברזל", "בידיהם")} "and iron mallets in their hands"; {SP_(198, 1, "שתחלת", "נפילה", "ניסה")} "for the beginning of defeat is flight"; {SP_(198, 1, "במלחמת", "הרשות")} "in an optional war"): THE CAPTAINS\' REAR GUARD (Sotah 8:6 the answer sheet) and the two wars named "optional" against "commanded" (190:17 named them "commanded" against "obligatory" — the vocabulary\'s dispute inside one spine, the English\'s notes) — the compile\'s war-kind parameter with both namings. Fresh.')
srow(199, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU DRAW NEAR TO A CITY" (20:10) — THE VERSE SPEAKS OF AN OPTIONAL WAR. ({SP_(199, 1, "במלחמת", "הרשות", "הכתוב", "מדבר")} "the verse speaks of an optional war"): the peace call scoped to the optional war (the seven nations\' cities at 20:16 without it — 201:1-2; Sifrei 251:1 this ledger\'s outside row denies it to Ammon and Moab) — the compile\'s scope. Fresh.')
srow(199, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO A CITY" — AND NOT TO A METROPOLIS. ({SP_(199, 2, "ולא", "לכרך")} "and not to a metropolis"): the city\'s class (180:1\'s form) — the compile\'s parameter on the besieged city. Fresh.')
srow(199, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO A CITY" — AND NOT TO A VILLAGE. ({SP_(199, 3, "ולא", "לכפר")} "and not to a village"): the lower bound. Fresh.')
srow(199, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO FIGHT AGAINST IT" — AND NOT TO STARVE IT, NOR TO MAKE IT THIRST, NOR TO KILL IT WITH DISEASE. ({SP_(199, 4, "ולא", "להרעיבה", "ולא", "להצמיאה")} "and not to starve it nor to make it thirst"; {SP_(199, 4, "מיתת", "תחלואים")} "death by disease"): THE MEANS BEFORE THE CALL — fighting only, no starvation (200:5 permits them AFTER the refusal): the compile\'s two-stage siege (before / after the peace call). Fresh.')
srow(199, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND CALL TO IT FOR PEACE" — GREAT IS PEACE: EVEN THE DEAD NEED PEACE; EVEN IN ISRAEL\'S WARS THEY NEED PEACE; THE DWELLERS ON HIGH NEED PEACE (JOB 25:2); THE PRIESTLY BLESSING CLOSES WITH PEACE; MOSES LOVED PEACE — "I SENT MESSENGERS FROM THE WILDERNESS OF KEDEMOT TO SIHON … WORDS OF PEACE" (2:26). ({SP_(199, 5, "גדול", "שלום")} "great is peace"; {SP_(199, 5, "ואף", "משה", "היה", "אוהב", "שלום")} "and Moses too was a lover of peace"): the peace litany (Sifrei Numbers 42\'s) with the tape\'s own Sihon line (2:26 — the readback\'s REFERENCE row for 20:10). REREAD WHOLE (chapters 1-3, deu_01_03_devarim).')
srow(200, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND IF IT ANSWERS YOU PEACE" (20:11) — MIGHT IT BE EVEN PART OF IT? THE TEACHING SAYS "AND OPENS TO YOU" — ALL OF IT AND NOT PART. ({SP_(200, 1, "יכול", "אף", "מקצתה")} "might it be even part of it?"; {SP_(200, 1, "כלה", "ולא", "מקצתה")} "all of it and not part of it"): THE PEACE UNANIMOUS — the whole city opens (a partial peace no peace) — the compile\'s condition on the answer. Fresh.')
srow(200, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND ALL THE PEOPLE FOUND IN IT" — TO INCLUDE THE CANAANITES INSIDE IT. ({SP_(200, 2, "לרבות", "כנענים", "שבתוכה")} "to include the Canaanites within it"): A CANAANITE IN A FAR CITY that makes peace LIVES as tribute — the herem does not reach him there (Sotah 35b, not opened) — the compile\'s cross-condition between the two war laws. Fresh.')
srow(200, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"THEY SHALL BE YOURS FOR TRIBUTE AND SERVE YOU" — IF THEY SAY "WE ACCEPT TRIBUTE BUT NOT SERVITUDE" OR "SERVITUDE BUT NOT TRIBUTE", THEY ARE NOT HEEDED UNTIL THEY ACCEPT BOTH. ({SP_(200, 3, "מסים", "ולא", "שעבוד")} "tribute and not servitude"; {SP_(200, 3, "עד", "שיקבלו", "עליהם", "זו", "וזו")} "until they accept upon themselves both"): THE TERMS BOTH — tribute and servitude a conjunction — the compile\'s peace verdict with two effects. Fresh.')
srow(200, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND IF IT MAKES NO PEACE WITH YOU AND MAKES WAR WITH YOU" (20:12) — THE VERSE TELLS YOU THAT IF IT MAKES NO PEACE, IN THE END IT MAKES WAR. ({SP_(200, 4, "לסוף", "שהיא", "עושה", "עמך", "מלחמה")} "in the end it makes war with you"): the refusal = war (the second arm entered) — the compile\'s condition. Fresh.')
srow(200, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND BESIEGE IT" — EVEN TO STARVE IT, EVEN TO MAKE IT THIRST, EVEN TO KILL IT WITH DISEASE. ({SP_(200, 5, "אף", "להרעיבה", "אף", "להצמיאה")} "even to starve it, even to make it thirst"): the means widened after the refusal (199:4\'s bar lifted) — the compile\'s second stage. Fresh.')
srow(200, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES IT INTO YOUR HAND" (20:13) — IF YOU DID ALL THAT IS SAID IN THE MATTER, IN THE END THE LORD GIVES IT INTO YOUR HAND. ({SP_(200, 6, "אם", "עשית", "את", "כל", "האמור", "בענין")} "if you did all that is said in the matter"): the victory conditioned on the procedure (184:1\'s form) — the compile\'s promise arm. Fresh.')
srow(200, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SMITE EVERY MALE BY THE SWORD" — I MIGHT HEAR EVEN THE LITTLE ONES INSIDE IT? THE TEACHING SAYS "ONLY THE WOMEN AND THE LITTLE ONES AND THE CATTLE" (20:14). OR ONLY THE FEMALE LITTLE ONES? YOU SAY: MIDIAN, WHERE THE GROWN WOMEN WERE KILLED, SPARED THE LITTLE GIRLS — HERE, WHERE THE GROWN WOMEN LIVE, SURELY THE LITTLE GIRLS? SO "LITTLE ONES" HERE IS THE MALE LITTLE ONES. WHENCE THE ONE WHO MAKES WAR WITH YOU? "ONLY THE WOMEN … ALL ITS SPOIL YOU SHALL TAKE" — MIGHT THEIR SPOIL BE FORBIDDEN TO YOU? "YOU SHALL TAKE AND EAT THE SPOIL OF YOUR ENEMIES". ({SP_(200, 7, "אף", "הקטנים", "שבתוכה")} "even the little ones inside it"; {SP_(200, 7, "ומה", "מדין")} "and what of Midian"; {SP_(200, 7, "טף", "של", "זכרים")} "the little ones of the males"; {SP_(200, 7, "תהא", "בזתם", "אסורה", "לך")} "might their spoil be forbidden to you"): THE MALES INCLUDING THE BOYS by the a-fortiori from Midian (Numbers 31:17-18 — the tape\'s own Midian lines; the refuge runner\'s neighbor num_31_midian the kin ledger) and THE SPOIL PERMITTED — the compile\'s siege verdict: males (all ages) by the sword, the women, children and spoil taken. Fresh.')
srow(201, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"SO SHALL YOU DO TO ALL THE FAR CITIES" (20:15) — THE FAR ONES ARE IN THIS LAW, THE NEAR ONES ARE NOT. ({SP_(201, 1, "הרחוקות", "בתורה", "הזאת")} "the far ones are in this law"; {SP_(201, 1, "ואין", "הקרובות", "בתורה", "הזאת")} "and the near ones are not in this law"): THE TWO CLASSES OF CITIES — far (the peace law) and near (the herem) — the compile\'s partition parameter (the seven nations\' land the "near"). Fresh.')
srow(201, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHICH ARE NOT OF THE CITIES OF THESE PEOPLES" — THE CITIES OF THESE NATIONS ARE NOT IN THIS LAW; "ONLY OF THE CITIES OF THESE PEOPLES YOU SHALL LET NO BREATH LIVE" (20:16) — BY THE SWORD. ({SP_(201, 2, "אין", "ערי", "הגוים", "האלה", "בתורה", "הזאת")} "the cities of these nations are not in this law"; {SP_(201, 2, "בסיף")} "by the sword"): THE HEREM\'S MODE the sword (the Mekhilta\'s "sword" the English\'s note) — the compile\'s effect on the seven nations\' cities (the cells of the seven-nations runner called with the receipt 20:17). Fresh.')
srow(201, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR YOU SHALL UTTERLY DESTROY THEM" (20:17) — MIGHT THEIR SPOIL BE FORBIDDEN TO YOU? THE TEACHING SAYS "AND HOUSES FULL OF EVERY GOOD THING" (6:11). ({SP_(201, 3, "יכול", "תהא", "בזתם", "אסורה", "לך")} "might their spoil be forbidden to you?"): THE HEREM\'S SPOIL PERMITTED by 6:11\'s promise (the tape\'s own line — chapter 6\'s sitting read this row) — the herem of persons, not of goods (Jericho\'s the exception, Joshua 6 — the Prophets\' case): the compile\'s spoil effect under the seven nations\' herem. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 6, deu_06_vaetchanan).')
srow(201, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE HITTITE AND THE AMORITE, THE CANAANITE AND THE PERIZZITE, THE HIVITE AND THE JEBUSITE" — WHEN IT SAYS "AS THE LORD YOUR GOD COMMANDED YOU" — TO INCLUDE THE GIRGASHITE. ({SP_(201, 4, "לרבות", "את", "הגרגשי")} "to include the Girgashite"): THE RECEIPT READ AS THE SEVENTH NATION — 20:17\'s six against 7:1\'s seven, "as He commanded you" supplying the Girgashite (the receipt Deut 20:17 — the register\'s line; the compile\'s pointer to 7:1 as the list\'s source, the dependency filed). Fresh.')
srow(202, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT THEY TEACH YOU NOT TO DO" (20:18) — THIS TEACHES THAT IF THEY REPENT THEY ARE NOT KILLED. ({SP_(202, 1, "שאם", "עושים", "תשובה", "אין", "נהרגים")} "that if they repent they are not killed"): THE HEREM\'S PURPOSE CLAUSE A CONDITION — the nations who repent live (Sotah 35b\'s three letters of Joshua, not opened; the Gibeonites the Prophets\' case) — the compile\'s condition on the seven nations\' cells (repentance = the abominations left). Fresh.')
srow(202, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SIN AGAINST THE LORD YOUR GOD" — IF YOU DID NOT DO ALL THAT IS SAID IN THE MATTER, YOU ARE CALLED SINNERS AGAINST THE LORD YOUR GOD. ({SP_(202, 2, "נקראים", "אתם", "חטאים")} "you are called sinners"): the omission\'s effect (200:6\'s form inverted) — the compile\'s sanction on the people. Fresh.')
srow(203, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU BESIEGE A CITY" (20:19) — THE VERSE SPEAKS OF AN OPTIONAL WAR. ({SP_(203, 1, "במלחמת", "הרשות", "הכתוב", "מדבר")} "the verse speaks of an optional war"): the trees\' law scoped like the peace call (199:1) — Fresh.')
srow(203, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO A CITY" — AND NOT TO A METROPOLIS. ({SP_(203, 2, "ולא", "לכרך")} "and not to a metropolis"): 199:2 at the trees. Fresh.')
srow(203, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO A CITY" — AND NOT TO A VILLAGE. ({SP_(203, 3, "ולא", "לכפר")} "and not to a village"): 199:3 at the trees. Fresh.')
srow(203, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"MANY DAYS" — DAYS, TWO; MANY, THREE. FROM HERE THEY SAID: ONE DOES NOT BESIEGE A CITY OF THE NATIONS LESS THAN THREE DAYS BEFORE THE SABBATH. ({SP_(203, 4, "ימים", "שנים", "רבים", "שלשה")} "days — two; many — three"; {SP_(203, 4, "פחות", "משלשה", "ימים", "קדם", "לשבת")} "less than three days before the Sabbath"): "MANY DAYS" = THREE (the count-word rule of 181:6\'s form) and the Sabbath\'s three-day rule (Shabbat 19a, not opened; the Tosefta the English\'s note) — the compile\'s siege timer keyed to the calendar\'s Sabbath. Fresh.')
srow(203, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO FIGHT AGAINST IT, TO SEIZE IT" — AND NOT TO TAKE IT CAPTIVE. ({SP_(203, 5, "ולא", "לשבותה")} "and not to take it captive"): the siege\'s aim seizure — the compile\'s note (the captive-taking of 21:10 a different verb). Fresh.')
srow(203, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT DESTROY ITS TREE BY SWINGING AN AX AGAINST IT" — I HAVE ONLY THE AX; TO DIVERT ITS WATER CHANNEL? "YOU SHALL NOT DESTROY ITS TREE" — BY ANY MEANS. ({SP_(203, 6, "למשך", "הימנה", "אמת", "המים")} "to draw off its water channel"; {SP_(203, 6, "בכל", "דבר")} "by any means"): THE BAR ON DESTRUCTION ANY MEANS (the ax the instance; Bava Kamma 91b\'s "do not destroy", not opened) — the compile\'s effect on the trees (the means parameter open). Fresh.')
srow(203, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "WHEN YOU BESIEGE A CITY" — IT TELLS THAT ONE DEMANDS PEACE TWO OR THREE DAYS BEFORE FIGHTING IT; "AND DAVID DWELT IN ZIKLAG TWO DAYS" (2 SAMUEL 1:1). ONE DOES NOT BEGIN A SIEGE ON THE SABBATH BUT THREE DAYS BEFORE; IF THEY SURROUNDED IT AND THE SABBATH CAME, THE SABBATH DOES NOT STOP THE WAR. THIS IS ONE OF THREE THINGS SHAMMAI THE ELDER EXPOUNDED: ONE DOES NOT SET SAIL ON THE GREAT SEA BUT THREE DAYS BEFORE THE SABBATH — FOR A FAR VOYAGE; FOR A NEAR ONE THEY SAIL. ({SP_(203, 7, "שתובע", "שלום", "שנים", "שלשה", "ימים")} "that one demands peace two or three days"; {SP_(203, 7, "אין", "השבת", "מפסקת", "מלחמתה")} "the Sabbath does not stop its war"; {SP_(203, 7, "שדרש", "שמי", "הזקן")} "that Shammai the Elder expounded"): THE PEACE DEMAND\'S DURATION two to three days and THE SABBATH\'S WAR CONTINUED (Shabbat 19a; the Tosefta Eruvin the English\'s notes) — the compile\'s two timers (the call\'s window; the Sabbath no interrupt); Shammai\'s ship the third thing beside. Fresh.')
srow(203, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR FROM IT YOU EAT" — A POSITIVE COMMANDMENT; "AND IT YOU SHALL NOT CUT" — A PROHIBITION. ({SP_(203, 8, "מצות", "עשה")} "a positive commandment"; {SP_(203, 8, "מצות", "לא", "תעשה")} "a prohibition"): the verse\'s two commandments (eat / cut not) — the compile\'s two effects on the fruit tree. Fresh.')
srow(203, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR IS THE TREE OF THE FIELD A MAN" — THIS TEACHES THAT MAN\'S LIFE IS ONLY FROM THE TREE. R. ISHMAEL: FROM HERE THE OMNIPRESENT SPARED THE TREE\'S FRUIT BY AN A-FORTIORI FROM THE TREE — IF THE TREE THAT MAKES FRUIT THE VERSE WARNED YOU ABOUT, THE FRUIT ITSELF HOW MUCH MORE! ({SP_(203, 9, "שחייו", "של", "אדם", "אינם", "אלא", "מן", "האילן")} "that a man\'s life is only from the tree"; {SP_(203, 9, "קל", "וחומר", "מאילן")} "an a-fortiori from the tree"): THE QUESTION READ AS A REASON ("for the tree is man\'s life" — Onkelos\'s statement the same way) and R. Ishmael\'s a-fortiori to the fruit — the compile\'s effect extended to the fruit (Bava Kamma 91b\'s bar on waste). Fresh.')
srow(203, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO COME BEFORE YOU IN THE SIEGE" — IF IT HINDERS YOU FROM COMING BEFORE YOU IN THE SIEGE, CUT IT. ({SP_(203, 10, "אם", "מעכבך")} "if it hinders you"; {SP_(203, 10, "קצצהו")} "cut it!"): THE EXCEPTION — a fruit tree that blocks the siege is cut — the compile\'s condition on the bar (the hindrance parameter). Fresh.')
srow(204, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"ONLY A TREE WHICH YOU KNOW" (20:20) — THIS IS A FRUIT TREE. ({SP_(204, 1, "זה", "אילן", "מאכל")} "this is a fruit tree"): the first clause read of the fruit tree that no longer bears (the English\'s bracket) — Fresh.')
srow(204, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT IT IS NOT A TREE FOR FOOD" — THIS IS A BARREN TREE. IF WE ARE TO INCLUDE THE FRUIT TREE, WHY "TREE FOR FOOD"? IT TEACHES THAT THE BARREN TREE COMES BEFORE THE FRUIT TREE. MIGHT IT BE EVEN ONE WORTH MORE IN MONEY, AS R. ELAZAR B. R. SHIMON SAYS? THE TEACHING SAYS "IT YOU SHALL DESTROY AND CUT". ({SP_(204, 2, "זה", "אילן", "סרק")} "this is a barren tree"; {SP_(204, 2, "שאילן", "סרק", "קודם", "לאילן", "מאכל")} "that the barren tree comes before the fruit tree"; {SP_(204, 2, "מעלה", "בדמים")} "worth more in money"): THE ORDER OF CUTTING — barren first, then fruit; R. Elazar b. R. Shimon\'s value exception denied (Bava Kamma 91b-92a, not opened) — the compile\'s ordering parameter. Fresh.')
srow(204, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'YOU MAKE OF IT BINS AND BOARDS. ({SP_(204, 3, "תיקים", "ונדביאות")} "bins and boards"): the cut wood\'s uses (the row with no citation in either file) — the compile\'s note. Fresh.')
srow(204, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND BUILD A SIEGE-WORK AGAINST THE CITY" — YOU MAKE AGAINST IT KINDS OF CATAPULTS. ({SP_(204, 4, "מיני", "מטרניאות")} "kinds of catapults"): the siege-work\'s machines (Greek loanwords) — the compile\'s note. Fresh.')
srow(204, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'YOU BRING AGAINST IT KINDS OF BALLISTAE. ({SP_(204, 5, "מיני", "בלסטראות")} "kinds of ballistae"): the second kind (no citation in either file). Fresh.')
srow(204, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"UNTIL IT FALLS" — EVEN ON THE SABBATH. ({SP_(204, 6, "ואפלו", "בשבת")} "and even on the Sabbath"): THE SIEGE OVERRIDES THE SABBATH (203:7\'s rule restated at the chapter\'s last words; Shabbat 19a) — the compile\'s Sabbath-override effect on the war\'s clock. Fresh.')
